  "xIPIOiu4VO4": { title: "We Need to Raise Young Men Who Can Support Themselves | From the Episode with Rabbi Raphael Kreuzer", description: "On October 8, 2023, while the fighting was still raging and the blood of our brothers and sisters had not yet dried, Rabbi Raphael Kreuzer published a searing post calling on yeshiva students to step up — not just to sit and learn, but to carry the burden, body and soul, as a first principle and not a last resort.\n\nRabbi Kreuzer came up through the elite Torah-study world of Yeshivas Chevron, a pillar of the Lithuanian (non-Hasidic) yeshiva world. In this conversation on \"Haredit Meduberet,\" he tells Esty Shushan about his worldview — speaking about moral rupture, about a Torah that demands real engagement with life itself, about the draft, about rabbinic courts, about leadership — and above all, about what happens when we forget why we were given the Torah in the first place." },
