  "FmSNBCfTR_I": { title: "Avigail Heilbron, Founder of Lo Tishtok, on the Struggle and the Reactions She Got From the Haredi Community", description: "Several years before #MeToo sparked a global reckoning, the Haredi community was undergoing an internal reckoning of its own. One post by Avigail Heilbron — a young Haredi woman working in high-tech — who chose to speak about her sense of safety, or the lack of it, set off a wave of disclosures from survivors, exposed a conspiracy of silence, and led to the founding of a movement, grassroots work on the ground, and a whole community shifting — and above all, a profound shift in awareness.\n\nChaim Walder, Yehuda Meshi-Zahav — these are just some of the names that came up at the time as examples of serial abusers, men with power and connections, whom the Haredi community cast out, though not without a fight.\n\nIn this episode of \"Haredit Meduberet,\" Esty Shushan talks with Avigail, founder of Lo Tishtok and co-director of Hineni, about the road she took, the costs and the challenges, about the complicated feminist identity that emerges in a young Haredi wife, about social media as an arena for struggle and change, about the silence of rabbinic leadership — and about the question of whether abusers can truly repent and be rehabilitated." },
